<p></p><center><table width=3D"610" border=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" cellpadd=
ing=3D"4">
  <tbody><tr>
    <td width=3D"100%" align=3D"CENTER" bgcolor=3D"#000000"><table width=3D=
"600" border=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"4">
        <tbody><tr>
          <td width=3D"100%" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff">
            <p></p><center><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/web/20050222=
044607im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/dcTitle.jpg" width=3D"576" =
height=3D"146" align=3D"BOTTOM" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"3"></center=
><p></p>

            <p></p><center><font size=3D"+3" face=3D"Times New Roman">Part =
II: We
            are Service of Borg</font></center><p></p>

            <p></p><center><i><font face=3D"Arial">(Almost everything in th=
is entire
            series is true. As the story progresses, I will let you, the
            reader, in on the things that didn't actually happen. Some, but
            not all, of the names have been changed.)</font></i></center><p=
></p>

            <p><b><font size=3D"+1" face=3D"Arial"><img src=3D"https://web.=
archive.org/web/20050222044607im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/DC0=
2T.gif" width=3D"56" height=3D"67" align=3D"LEFT" border=3D"0" naturalsizef=
lag=3D"3"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/web/20050222044607im_/http://=
hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/dcauthor.jpg" width=3D"201" height=3D"94" al=
ign=3D"RIGHT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"3"></font><font face=3D"Arial=
">he condition
            of my exhaust system was yielding unprecedented low mileage.
            We had to stop at the next town, Troy, Pennsylvania. I pulled
            into the station just off the exit and started to get out of
            the car when I was approached by something half-man, half-machi=
ne.
            Startled and scared, I ducked back into my sedan.</font></b></p=
>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/=
web/20050222044607im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/dc02borg.jpg" w=
idth=3D"276" height=3D"431" align=3D"LEFT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"=
3">He was
            pale, mid-forties, about 5' 8", 180 lbs. with an added 40
            lbs. or so of electronics strapped to his body. A small view
            screen covered his right eye, supplying information privy only
            to the left side of his brain. Soft beeps and blips emanated
            from him as he stepped closer to my window, and they tingled
            like techno-wind chimes amongst the swelling breeze of the high=
way,
            now seemingly worlds away.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">A midget appeared from nowhere, craw=
led
            onto my car's hood and started to squeegee the bugs off my wind=
shield.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Fill 'er up?" the cyborg
            inquired in a ghastly jolly voice as he adjusted the brim of
            his baseball cap which sported the logo of the station.</font><=
/b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Uh, yeah," I managed to say
            while in complete shock. I don't know what surprised me more,
            the alien nature of the attendants, or the alien idea of a full
            service gas station.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">The cyborg turned towards the multi-=
nozzled
            pump. "Regular?"</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">I thought that was a strange questio=
n
            to ask, but not knowing how full-service "full-service"
            could mean, I decided to lie in order to avoid unwanted colon
            hydrotherapy.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Yep, once a day, everyday! Sometime=
s
            twice!"</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">The midget laughed a full-bodied lau=
gh,
            lost his footing and rolled down the hood, making a small thud
            on the pavement.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/=
web/20050222044607im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/DC02MAP.jpg" wi=
dth=3D"360" height=3D"355" align=3D"RIGHT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"=
3">"I'm
            all right!" He informed the world in a spirited voice. He
            revived quickly, sprang up to the roof of the car and started
            to work on the rear window.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">The human parts of the cyborg seemed
            pleased in his co-worker's well-being, and began the transfer
            of 87 octane petroleum fluids in the same way that I have done
            countless times before.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">Upon completion, the attendant retur=
ned
            to my window.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"That'll be $21.35," he read
            from the pump. This made me wonder what the monocular view scre=
en
            was showing him. Jason later told me he assumed it was a connec=
tion
            to the Internet via the satellite transponder poking out of his
            backpack, and that it was probably streaming, directly to the
            brain, 1000's of images per hour of Star-Trek based homoerotica=
.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">I gave him my gas card which he ran
            quickly along a groove in the right side of his belt. He pulled
            a pad attached to him by a spiral cord from a compartment by
            his chest and handed me something that looked like a pen, but
            had no ink.<br>
            "Sign here," he pointed to a glass plate underneath
            a red LED readout glowing "$21.35."</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">I signed, and the receipt rolled out
            of a box attached to his left thigh. He handed it to me. My sig=
nature
            was already on it.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Thank you. Have a nice day,"
            he said as his one visible eye sparkled.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Domo Arigoto, Mister Roboto."
            I pulled out onto the road and then back to what I thought to
            be route 14, narrowly missing the midget, who now appeared to
            be over five and a half feet tall.<br>
            </font></b></p>

            <p></p><center><b><font face=3D"Arial"><br>
            <hr></font></b></center><p></p>

            <p></p><center><a href=3D"https://web.archive.org/web/200502220=
44607/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/Stories/dc03.html"><b><font face=3D"Ar=
ial">PART III:
            If I Could Put Lime in a Bottle.</font></b></a></center><p></p>

